---

For the statistical analysis I need every game's `actualTuple` vs `predictedTuple`. The harness emits those (to stderr) for each of the ~652 games where the picker disagrees with history; the ~280 that match are ties by definition. Run this to capture the lot:

```
! RUN_PICKER_INTEGRATION=true op run --env-file ./.env -- npx vitest run --config vitest.picker.integration.config.ts > /Users/toastboy/.claude/jobs/d1b14dd8/tmp/parity_full.txt 2>&1; echo done
```

It's a big file (~650 JSON diagnostic blocks). I'll parse all of them and give you aggregate tables — mean/median Δaverage, Δage, Δgoalies, Δunknown-age for historical vs picker splits, how often the picker's split dominates, and how far each sits from the theoretical optimum (`bestTuple`).

